 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Launch at 30°",
   "text": "A ball is launched at \\( v_i = 20 \\) m s⁻¹ and \\( \\theta = {{th|0}}^\\circ \\). Press play and note where it lands.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 0,
      "tm": 0,
      "th": 30
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "tm": 2.2
     },
     "at": 100,
     "dur": 2600
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Complementary angle",
   "text": "Now add the angle \\( 90^\\circ - \\theta = 60^\\circ \\): a **higher, longer** flight that lands at the **same point**.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 1,
      "tm": 0,
      "th": 30
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "tm": 4
     },
     "at": 100,
     "dur": 5500
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Why the same range?",
   "text": "Because \\( \\sin 2\\theta = \\sin(180^\\circ - 2\\theta) \\). The graph of \\( R \\) against \\( \\theta \\) is symmetric about 45°, so \\( \\theta \\) and \\( 90^\\circ - \\theta \\) share the same height on it.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 2,
      "tm": 4,
      "th": 30
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "The best angle",
   "text": "The peak of the curve is at **45°**: \\( R_{max} = v_i^2/g \\). Move \\( \\theta \\) to 45° and the two paths merge.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 3,
      "tm": 0,
      "th": 45
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "tm": 3
     },
     "at": 200,
     "dur": 4200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "Highest and farthest",
   "text": "At 45° the maximum height is \\( H = R/4 \\), so \\( R_{max} = 4H \\).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 3,
      "tm": 3,
      "th": 45
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
